{
 "_source": "Every rule and number the training salon runs on, in one place. Read by website/_src/salon.py (pages) and copied by build.py to site/api/_lib/salon/policy.json (the booking engine cannot read _data/ at run time). Change a value here, rebuild, and it changes on the pages and in the engine together.",
 "_todo_pm": "A value written as {\"todo_pm\": true, \"value\": X} is a PLACEHOLDER the PM has not confirmed. While ANY remain: the salon pages are built noindex and left out of the sitemap, prices and opening times are shown as 'to be confirmed', and the booking engine refuses to take a booking in production. To confirm a value, replace the whole object with the plain value (2.0, not {\"todo_pm\": true, \"value\": 2.0}).",
 "_units": "Money is whole pounds. Times are minutes, or HH:MM clock times in Europe/London. Service timings are the minutes a QUALIFIED stylist takes; a learner's level factor multiplies the 'work' and 'basin' parts only — developing time ('process') and the supervisor's check ('check') do not stretch.",
